+<!-- MOCK-HOOK FILE: the plugins console mock-ups' inventory (lane PLUGINS-CONSOLE-MOCKUPS, step foundation). -->
+# The plugins console: every item each direction must place
+
+Read on main at f85da72, 4 November 2026. Each line: an id (the scaffold marks the element that carries it with
+`data-f="<id>"`), the item, and where it comes from. "Design" is `docs/design/agent-plugins.md`, "Bridge" is
+`docs/design/agent-plugins-question-bridge.md`. **Not served** means main has no field for it yet; the fixture invents
+the smallest honest shape (base-notes.md, "Shapes not built yet").
+
+## 1. Config › Plugins (admin)
+
+| id | Item | Comes from |
+|---|---|---|
+| C1 | The plugin's name (gstack) | `GET /v1/workspaces/{t}/plugins` → `catalogue[].name` (`swarm_api/plugins.py` `catalogue_view`); Design, "A closed plugin catalogue" |
+| C2 | Its pinned version (1.92.55.0), fixed in the image, never chosen by a person | `catalogue[].version` (`plugincatalogue.GSTACK`); Design, "Packaging: baked in, pinned" |
+| C3 | The runner profiles it supports (the five claude-code profiles) | `catalogue[].runner_profiles` (`CLAUDE_CODE_PROFILES`) |
+| C4 | Per mode (unattended, planner, designer), the skills it may offer | `catalogue[].modes[mode].skills`; Design, the table "Mode / Skills offered" |
+| C5 | What each skill does, in a few words | **Not served**: fixture `skillNotes`, worded from gstack's skill descriptions as the design doc summarises them |
+| C6 | Whether each mode runs today, and if not why (planner and designer wait for the question bridge) | `catalogue[].modes[mode].available` / `.reason` (`BRIDGE_REASON`) |
+| C7 | The never-offered skills, each shown as such with why (`careful`, `guard`, `cso`, `gstack-upgrade`, ...) | **Not served**: fixture `neverOffered`, from Design "Never offered" and `plugins.py` (cso left out, 3 Nov) |
+| C8 | The workspace setting: which catalogue plugins this workspace may use | `plugins.allowed` (`PluginsStore`, `workspace_settings/{t}.plugins`) |
+| C9 | The default when nobody chose: none allowed | `defaults.plugins.allowed` (`DEFAULT_ALLOWED = ()`) |
+| C10 | Changing it: admin only (workspace owner or admin, or a platform admin) | `can_edit`; `PUT /v1/workspaces/{t}/plugins` `{allowed}` (`authorize_write`) |
+| C11 | Signed: only a block whose MAC verifies allows anything; an unsigned list allows nothing | `plugins.py` module doc, `allowed_plugins` (the read serves signed names only; no "signed" flag is served) |
+| C12 | Audited: who changed it and when (last change, and the changes before it) | `set_by`, `set_at`; audit row `workspace_plugins_set` (**the history is not served** by this route: fixture `changes`) |
+| C13 | A viewer sees it all read only, told why they cannot change it | `can_edit: false` (`authorize_read` lets every member read) |
+| C14 | Chosen by name only: no path, command, URL or version is taken from a person | Invariant 10; `PluginsPut` takes `allowed` names only; `catalogue_view` does not serve the install path |
+
+## 2. The step's plugin picker in the workflow builder
+
+| id | Item | Comes from |
+|---|---|---|
+| B1 | On one step: choose a plugin from the catalogue | `SubmitWorkflow.tsx` step editor; sent as `metadata.work_contract.capabilities.plugins` (`plugins.FIELD_PATH`) |
+| B2 | Its mode: unattended, planner or designer | `capabilities.plugins.<name>.mode` (`plugincatalogue.MODES`) |
+| B3 | The skills it may use, from what the catalogue offers for that mode | `capabilities.plugins.<name>.skills`; `check_step` refuses a skill the mode does not offer |
+| B4 | Only plugins the workspace allowed are offered as choosable | `GET /v1/plugins` → `plugins.allowed` |
+| B5 | Refusal, said plainly: this step's runner profile cannot load plugins | `check_step`: "gstack runs only on the profiles ..., not <profile>" |
+| B6 | Refusal, said plainly: the workspace has not allowed it (and who can) | `check_step`: "this workspace has not allowed gstack: its owner or admin allows it ..." |
+| B7 | Refusal: a mode that does not run yet (planner, designer until the bridge lands) | `check_step` / `catalogue[].modes[m].available: false` with `reason` |
+| B8 | The chosen set shown compactly on the step afterwards | `SubmitWorkflow.tsx` step card; `RunnerPicker.tsx` `StepRunnerFacts` sits beside it |
+| B9 | On a finished step, what it actually used: plugin, version, mode, skills | attempt `result_summary.plugins.<name>` `{version, mode, skills}` (`agent_worker/plugins.record`) |
+| B10 | How many times each skill ran (0 is a measured zero; not read is shown as not known) | `result_summary.plugins.<name>.skill_runs` |
+| B11 | The submission's own refusal, on the step it names | 422 `validation_failed`, `detail.plugins = "plugin_refused"`, `detail.step_id` (`plugins._refuse`) |
+
+## 3. The interview on the planning page (planner and designer modes)
+
+| id | Item | Comes from |
+|---|---|---|
+| I1 | The pending question's text | `GET /v1/tasks/{id}/questions` → `questions[i].question` (a bridged `question_wait`) |
+| I2 | Its options (label and description) | `questions[i].options[]` |
+| I3 | The recommended option, marked | `questions[i].recommended` (the CLI's "(Recommended)" label convention; Bridge, finding 3) |
+| I4 | Each option's preview: text, a diagram, or a rendered HTML design | Hook payload `options[].preview` (Bridge, finding 3); **not served** by the read: fixture `previews` |
+| I5 | The skill that asked | **Not served** (not in the hook payload; Bridge, finding 3 and "Unknowns"): fixture `skill` |
+| I6 | The questions answered so far | **Not served whole**: `metadata.question_waits_earlier` keeps 5 (`MAX_EARLIER_WAITS`): fixture `interview` |
+| I7 | Who answered each | `answer.by` |
+| I8 | Where each was answered: the console, Voice it, Claude Code | `answer.via` (`console`, `claude-code`, `github-comment` on main; **`voice-it` not built**: fixture) |
+| I9 | "Use the recommended answer" | `POST /v1/tasks/{id}/answers` with `choice = recommended` |
+| I10 | An answer in the person's own words | `POST .../answers` `text`; `question_bridge.answer_message` marks it as the person's own words |
+| I11 | How long it waits: 24 hours from when it was asked, then the step ends with the question left open, never answered for anyone | `waiting.asked_at`, `waiting.expires_at` (`BRIDGE_WAIT_MAX_SECONDS`) |
+| I12 | The first answer stands; a second is refused | 409 `already_answered` (`agent_questions.ALREADY_ANSWERED`) |
+| I13 | While it waits the step is parked: no lease, no slot, no container | Design, "The question bridge" step 2; invariant 1 |
+| I14 | The step's plugin context: plugin, version, mode, skills it may use | step `capabilities.plugins`; catalogue version |
+| I15 | Interview progress: how many answered; how many are left is not known | count of `interview`; the total is the agent's, never served |
+| I16 | The proposal when the interview ends: plan, design doc, diagrams | `IssueRun.plan` (`RunPlan`) on main; design doc and diagrams **not served**: fixture `proposal` |
+| I17 | Approve, Edit or Reject against the plan's digest | `Runs.tsx` plan decision (`approveRun` / `editRunPlan` / `rejectRun`, `plan_digest`) |
+| I18 | Or approved automatically when the run asks for that | `IssueRun.plan_approval: 'auto'` |
+
+## 4. Needs you (owner questions)
+
+| id | Item | Comes from |
+|---|---|---|
+| N1 | The interview's pending question as a parked step in Needs you | `work/NeedsYou.tsx` `QuestionNeed`; the bridged wait parks the step |
+| N2 | An unattended step's unanswerable question parks there too | Design, "Unattended" decision; `agent_questions.py` "A PLUGIN STEP'S QUESTION" |
+| N3 | Answer in the row, or open the planning page for the previews | `NeedsYou` Answer opens the box in the row (`answerQuestion`) |
+| N4 | Its expiry (24 hours) and that nothing is answered for anyone | `waiting.expires_at` |
+| N5 | Which plugin, mode and skill asked | step `capabilities.plugins`; fixture `skill` |
